---
description: Read the Greptile context files for paths the diff touches.
alwaysApply: true
---

Greptile id: files-json
Severity: context
Scope: the paths listed below (from .greptile/files.json)

`.greptile/files.json` attaches context rather than extra rule text. Cursor rules cannot attach those files automatically. When a review touches a listed scope, read the file and apply it.

- `docs/review-rules.md` — every review. Review rubric, blockers, evidence, and how to write findings.
- `CONTRIBUTING.md` — every review. Pull request scope, verification, and changelog requirements.
- `AGENTS.md` — when the diff touches `src/**`, `test/**`, `package.json`, or `scripts/**`. Provider architecture, protocol constraints, and release gates.
- `docs/cache-log-runbook.md` — when the diff touches `src/context/**`, `src/session.ts`, `src/language-model.ts`, `src/protocol/**`, `src/billing.ts`, or `src/usage.ts`.
- `docs/host-compat-acceptance.md` — when the diff touches `src/protocol/create-plan.ts`, `src/protocol/switch-mode.ts`, `src/host-agent-mode.ts`, `src/host-plan-file.ts`, or `src/context/**`.

There is no `.greptile/rules.md` and no root `greptile.json` in this repository. `.greptile/config.json` is the rule source.
